# behavior 1
# name: buffer_concurrent_passages_stay_contiguous
# provenance: CRDT_ENGINE_SPEC.md requires a producer's inserted passage to stay
#   contiguous; evaluation finding F8 reports that concurrent passages interleave
#   character by character. Fixed by S01-S07, which are not implemented.
# status: known-defect
# scope: multiple producers, buffer
# expect converged yes
# expect contains_of 0 68656c6c6f
# expect contains_of 0 776f726c64
# note: two producers each insert a passage at position 0 of an empty document.
#   Which passage lands first is unspecified, so the expectation is that each
#   survives as a contiguous run rather than interleaved per character — today's
#   behaviour interleaves them, which is what F8 names.
#collabtext-trace 1
#model buffer
#label f8-concurrent-passages
#seed 42
#replicas 2
#net 50 200 500 1
edit 0 0 0 68656c6c6f
edit 1 0 0 776f726c64
deliver 1 0
deliver 0 1
